<title>JAPAN: Japan April current account surplus jumps 93 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan April current account surplus jumps 93 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The surplus in Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, rose 92.7 percent to 1.09 trillion yen in April from a year earlier, the Ministry of Finance (MOF) announced on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The surplus in merchandise trade alone rose 90.9 percent to 1.02 trillion yen from the same month a year earlier, the ministry said.</p>
